### IozyCore - test requests
### Prerequisite: `docker compose up --build` must be running (API on localhost:8080)
### With VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request"
### above each block. With IntelliJ/DataGrip: open this file as it is.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api

### 0. DO THIS FIRST - the API has required a session since 2026-08-29.
### Without it, all the requests below answer 401. The HTTP client
### then keeps the session cookie and sends it back by itself.
###
### On a new instance (no account), use `register`: it creates the
### account, logs it in at the same time, and this first account TAKES OVER the
### collection already in the database. On an instance already in use, use `login`.
### Check which one with /auth/etat.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/etat

### 0bis. Create the first account (new instance only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "moi@example.com",
  "motDePasse": "un-mot-de-passe",
  "pseudo": "moi"
}

### 0ter. Log in (instance already in use)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "moi@example.com",
  "motDePasse": "un-mot-de-passe"
}

### 1. Quick add of a manga (flow 1) - UUID = EntityType.MANGA (see EntityType.java)
### Response: { "entityId": "...", "matchedExistingEntity": false } - replace
### REMPLACER_PAR_UUID_RETOURNE below with the value of entityId.
# @name quickAddManga
POST {{baseUrl}}/entities/quick-add
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entityTypeId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "title": "Death Note - Tome 1",
  "condition": "NEW"
}

### 1bis. Replay EXACTLY the same request - must return "matchedExistingEntity": true
### with the same entityId (UC1 deduplication), and a 2nd Ownership is created for this same Entity.
POST {{baseUrl}}/entities/quick-add
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entityTypeId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "title": "death note - tome 1",
  "condition": "USED"
}

### 2. Read the Entity that was created (replace {{id}} with the UUID returned above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/entities/REMPLACER_PAR_UUID_RETOURNE

### 3. Check the status before buying (flow 3) - must return OWNED right after step 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/wishlist/lookup?entityId=REMPLACER_PAR_UUID_RETOURNE

### 4. Record an Experience (UC3) - "READ" is allowed for the MANGA type
POST {{baseUrl}}/experiences
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entityId": "REMPLACER_PAR_UUID_RETOURNE",
  "experienceType": "READ",
  "occurredAt": "2026-07-30",
  "rating": 9,
  "comment": "Excellent premier tome"
}

### 5. Try an Experience type that is not allowed (must return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/experiences
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entityId": "REMPLACER_PAR_UUID_RETOURNE",
  "experienceType": "PLAYED",
  "occurredAt": "2026-07-30",
  "rating": 5,
  "comment": "Ne devrait pas passer"
}

### 6. Create a Tag and link it to the Entity
POST {{baseUrl}}/tags
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "seinen"
}

### 7. Note: quick-add always creates an Entity + its Ownership together
### (see QuickAddService.java). There is no endpoint yet to
### create a "bare" Entity to add directly to the wishlist without
### owning it - to add if this use case is a priority for you.
### Meanwhile, /api/wishlist expects an entityId of an Entity that already
### exists (found through a search, for example).

### 8. Try to delete the manga Entity created at step 1 (must return 409 Conflict,
### because its Ownership still exists)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/entities/REMPLACER_PAR_UUID_RETOURNE

### 9. Read the automatically generated OpenAPI documentation
GET http://localhost:8080/v3/api-docs

### 10. Search manga metadata through Jikan (Metadata Enrichment)
GET {{baseUrl}}/metadata/search?entityTypeId=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001&query=Death Note

### 11. Search board game metadata through BGG (Metadata Enrichment)
GET {{baseUrl}}/metadata/search?entityTypeId=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003&query=Catan

### 12. Find a manga from a scanned ISBN (Open Library, no key required)
GET {{baseUrl}}/metadata/lookup-barcode?entityTypeId=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001&barcode=9782723492607

### 13. Quick add with pre-filled attributes (from a candidate chosen at step 10)
POST {{baseUrl}}/entities/quick-add
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entityTypeId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "title": "Death Note",
  "condition": "NEW",
  "attributes": {
    "mangaka": "Ohba, Tsugumi",
    "publisher": "Weekly Shonen Jump"
  }
}

### 14. Bulk import your BGG collection (games marked "owned" only)
### Replace "someuser" with a real BGG username. It may take a few seconds
### (BGG sometimes answers 202 while it prepares the export - handled automatically
### with a retry on the backend side). Response: { totalFound, created, matchedExisting, failed }
POST {{baseUrl}}/metadata/bgg/import?username=someuser

### 15. List all board games (used by the iOS app to refresh the Shelves after a BGG import)
GET {{baseUrl}}/entities?entityTypeId=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003

### 16. Cross-search in your collection (UC4) - all types together
GET {{baseUrl}}/entities/search?q=death

### 17. Cross-search filtered by type (mangas only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/entities/search?entityTypeId=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### 18. Collection statistics (UC6) - number of entities/ownerships per type,
### average rating, experiences of the current year, most used tags
GET {{baseUrl}}/insights/stats

### 19. Manga discovery - other works by the same author as your best rated mangas
GET {{baseUrl}}/insights/discover?entityTypeCode=MANGA

### 20. Board game discovery - BGG trending games sharing categories/mechanics
### with yours (needs owned games with a captured bggId - through search
### or collection import)
GET {{baseUrl}}/insights/discover?entityTypeCode=BOARD_GAME

### 21. Search video game metadata through IGDB (needs IGDB_CLIENT_ID/SECRET
### configured in .env - otherwise returns an empty list, see README)
GET {{baseUrl}}/metadata/search?entityTypeId=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002&query=zelda

### 22. Video game discovery - games similar (IGDB similar_games) to yours
### (needs owned games with a captured igdbId, and configured IGDB credentials)
GET {{baseUrl}}/insights/discover?entityTypeCode=VIDEO_GAME

### 23. Dynamic type editor - list all types (the 3 historical ones + any created type)
GET {{baseUrl}}/entity-types

### 24. Create a custom type (code normalised to UPPER_SNAKE_CASE on the server)
POST {{baseUrl}}/entity-types
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "films",
  "label": "Films",
  "allowedExperienceTypes": ["WATCHED"],
  "customFieldKeys": ["director"]
}

### 25. Try to delete a type still used by an Entity (must return 409 Conflict)
### Replace with the id of a type that is really referenced, e.g. MANGA if step 1 was played.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/entity-types/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
